  "goodToKnow": "Die Notwehr is self-defence in law: in Notwehr handeln. Under § 32 of the criminal code, an act necessary to repel a present, unlawful attack on oneself or others is not unlawful. German law is relatively generous: Das Recht braucht dem Unrecht nicht zu weichen (right need not yield to wrong). Exceeding it out of fear is called Notwehrexzess. Die Wehr means defence. It has no plural."
